{"kind":"artifact","text":"GitHub connector HTTP hardening is ready for independent review at exact head 7a717feea7fe9d02026cce1e89100b5b2318212f. Decoded response bodies are capped at 8 MiB for both reads and pull-request responses with an explicit over-limit error; issue observation stops at 100 pages or 10,000 raw API records before pull-request filtering and logs the known omitted records plus unfetched later pages; and the connector clones its configured HTTP client and unconditionally refuses redirects before a bearer token can be forwarded. Tests cover gzip expansion past the decoded limit, bounded POST responses, PR-only endless pagination, an oversized first batch, and same-host HTTPS-to-HTTP plus unrelated-host redirect attempts under an injected permissive redirect policy. Architecture remains inside the application connector layer; kernel, application host, fold, and connector charter contracts are unchanged. Verified: go test ./internal/connector/github; go test -race ./internal/connector/github; make test; make race; go vet ./...; make build; git diff --check; clean tracked worktree. Branch request/github-http-bounds-v2 is pushed to origin.","body":{"branch":"request/github-http-bounds-v2","commit":"7a717feea7fe9d02026cce1e89100b5b2318212f","path":"internal/connector/github","tests":"go test ./internal/connector/github; go test -race ./internal/connector/github; make test; make race; go vet ./...; make build; git diff --check"}}